  "question": {
    "text": "In an experiment with photoelectric effect, the stopping potential,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "83FjV",
      "text": "increases with increase in the intensity of the incident light",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4ZL0c",
      "text": "decreases with increase in the intensity of the incident light",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Mc6Lo",
      "text": "increases with increase in the wavelength of the incident light",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AxRPB",
      "text": "is $\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}}\\right)$ times the maximum kinetic energy of the emitted photoelectrons",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From Einstein photoelectric equation\n$\\frac{h c}{\\lambda}=\\phi+e V_S$\n\nMaximum K.E. $=(\\mathrm{K})_{\\max }=e V s$\nSo, $V_S=\\frac{(\\mathrm{K})_{\\max }}{e}$",
    "image": null
  },
